{"skill":{"slug":"vercel-deployment","displayName":"Vercel"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1772058076403,"changelog":"Auto-publish from CI","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":779,"sha256":"0fdd8ba0ce66fee293b2c682b126b40979fe87ea23e6b55dfffa013e46009e6b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1503,"sha256":"35530587795a607350184b473529213042fb308aa52f6c52215a5c61f0a18c55","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789086163407,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bb853b984a2637879f85695e1ec3fda02e30762814621f1e02b16fcd56e28644","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bb853b984a2637879f85695e1ec3fda02e30762814621f1e02b16fcd56e28644","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: vercel-deployment\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle primarily uses standard `npx vercel` commands for project deployment and management. While the commands themselves are legitimate, the `SKILL.md` file contains instructions that require the AI agent to substitute user-provided values (e.g., `<project-root>`, `VAR_NAME`, `value`). This creates a significant prompt injection vulnerability, as an attacker could craft malicious inputs for these placeholders, potentially leading to shell injection or unauthorized actions if the agent does not properly sanitize or validate them before execution. There is no direct evidence of intentional malicious code or data exfiltration within the provided files, but the potential for exploitation via prompt injection makes it suspicious.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779167233862},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":24,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789086163407},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a short Vercel deployment guide whose sensitive actions are disclosed and purpose-aligned, though users should pin the CLI and use scoped credentials.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Vercel account, repository, domain, and production env-var access is proportionate for deployment management but should be limited to the intended project.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install scripts or bundled executable code were present; runtime examples use unpinned `npx vercel`, which may download and execute the current CLI version.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The commands are manual examples, not hidden automation, but they can change deployment settings and production environment variables.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No local persistence, services, hooks, or memory writes were found; `vercel git connect` intentionally creates an ongoing auto-deploy integration.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill describes Vercel project setup, repository connection, environment variables, and domain listing, which match its stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing or using this skill, prefer a pinned or project-local Vercel CLI, verify the Vercel project and Git repository before connecting auto-deploys, and use least-privilege Vercel credentials when adding production environment variables.","findings":"[RP1] expected: Confirmed multiple unpinned `npx vercel` examples. This is a real supply-chain caution, especially for env-var handling, but it is visible, purpose-aligned, and not evidence of malicious behavior in the artifact.\n[EA2] expected: The `git connect` auto-deploy setup is disclosed and central to Vercel use. The artifact does not instruct the agent to run it without user direction.\n[T08] expected: The static warning about unpinned Vercel CLI execution is supported by the skill text; it warrants user guidance rather than a Review verdict because no deceptive or unrelated dependency behavior was found.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789086163407}}}}}